        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12546788/comment/13232529",
          "id": "13232529",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "> What is your use case, that is, why do you need getAllNodeIds? I'm just wondering if we really need this method... If we could remove it then we wouldn't have to deal with such problems. \n\nIt's needed by the datastore garbage collector and the consistency checker.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2012-03-19T09:52:30.647+0000",
          "updated": "2012-03-19T09:52:30.647+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12546788/comment/13232540",
          "id": "13232540",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=unico%40apache.org",
            "name": "unico@apache.org",
            "key": "unico@apache.org",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Unico Hommes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "I was using the Jackrabbit consistency checker. See http://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/jackrabbit/tags/2.4.0/jackrabbit-core/src/main/java/org/apache/jackrabbit/core/persistence/bundle/ConsistencyCheckerImpl.java\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=unico%40apache.org",
            "name": "unico@apache.org",
            "key": "unico@apache.org",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Unico Hommes",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2012-03-19T10:43:57.073+0000",
          "updated": "2012-03-19T10:43:57.073+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12546788/comment/13232556",
          "id": "13232556",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "OK I see. For data store garbage collection, you could live without the method, as persistence manager scan is optional there. But the consistency checker needs it, and changing the consistency checker to do a regular node traversal would be probably quite a lot of work.\n\nNot sure how to solve it, possibly use \"order by desc\"? I guess more tests would be required (it seems we use varbinary(16) in MySQL, which might deal with trailing zeroes differently and binary(16))",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2012-03-19T11:00:07.439+0000",
          "updated": "2012-03-19T11:00:07.439+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12546788/comment/13232558",
          "id": "13232558",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=unico%40apache.org",
            "name": "unico@apache.org",
            "key": "unico@apache.org",
            "avatarUrls": {
